/*
:name: undefined_generic_arg
:type: error
:error: unknown type or lambda 'ZZ' in a generic argument
:help: declare `ZZ` before its use
*/

// Ruling 2026-09-28 #24 (clarification): reading a name with no accessible
// declaration is a direct compile error at the read. A call-site generic bind
// passes a bare name through for the runner to bind; before, an undeclared
// name became nil and surfaced only as the indirect upass.tolg "unresolved
// reference 'inl1_ZZ'".
// User ruling 2026-09-28 (33): the error names what a generic argument reads (a
// type, lambda or comptime const declared earlier), not a variable.
comb addn<N=1>(a:U8) -> (r:U8) {
  r = (a + N)#[0..<8]
}

pub comb undefined_generic_arg(a:U8) -> (r:U8) {
  r = addn<N=ZZ>(a=a)  // locate_error_here
}
